<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => (element == null && this.get(index) == null) || this.get(index).equals(element);</code>

This assertion ensures that if the index is within the valid range, then either the added element is null and the element at the index is also null, or the element at the index after the addition equals the added element.--------------------<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => (element == null && this.get(index) == null) || this.get(index).equals(element);</code>--------------------<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => (element == null && this.get(index) == null) || this.get(index).equals(element);</code>

This assert statement checks that if the index is within the valid range (from 0 to the old size of the list), then either the added element is null and the element at the specified index is also null, or the element at the specified index after the addition equals the added element.--------------------